      "name": "webhook",
      "type": "registry:item",
      "title": "WhatsApp webhook",
      "description": "Next.js route for the WhatsApp Cloud API webhook plus the Sendo client config (Supabase adapter, Meta direct transport).",
      "dependencies": ["@quami/sendo", "@supabase/supabase-js"],
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "registry/items/webhook/app/api/sendo/webhook/route.ts",
          "type": "registry:page",
          "target": "app/api/sendo/webhook/route.ts"
        },
        {
          "path": "registry/items/webhook/lib/sendo.ts",
          "type": "registry:lib",
          "target": "lib/sendo.ts"
        },
        {
          "path": "registry/items/webhook/AGENTS.md",
          "type": "registry:file",
          "target": "components/sendo/webhook/AGENTS.md"
        }
      ],
      "envVars": {
        "SENDO_META_APP_SECRET": "",
        "SENDO_VERIFY_TOKEN": "",
        "SENDO_TOKEN_MAIN": "",
        "SENDO_AGENT_MODEL": "",
        "NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL": "",
        "SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY": "",
        "SENDO_STORAGE_BUCKET": "sendo-media",
        "SENDO_CONNECT_API_KEY": "",
        "SENDO_CONNECT_SIGNING_SECRET": ""
      },
      "docs": "Sendo webhook installed. In Meta App Dashboard > WhatsApp > Configuration set the Callback URL to https://<your-domain>/api/sendo/webhook and the Verify token to SENDO_VERIFY_TOKEN, then subscribe to the \"messages\" field. Each sendo_accounts.token_ref names the env var holding that number's access token (e.g. SENDO_TOKEN_MAIN). Install @sendo/schema for the database, then run `npx @quami/sendo doctor`. Using Sendo Connect instead of your own Meta app: set SENDO_CONNECT_API_KEY and SENDO_CONNECT_SIGNING_SECRET, register the same URL in the Connect panel and uncomment `connect` in lib/sendo.ts (leave the SENDO_CONNECT_* vars empty otherwise). See components/sendo/webhook/AGENTS.md."
    },
