      "docs": "Sendo inbox installed at /inbox (app/(protected)/inbox). It needs @sendo/webhook (lib/sendo.ts) and @sendo/schema (v2). Before using it: (1) implement requireUser() in app/(protected)/inbox/inbox-config.ts with your app's auth (it throws until then, so the inbox fails closed) and return the operator's tenant; (2) configure resolveRole (and resolveUsers / resolveAssignees) in lib/sendo.ts: users without a role see \"You don't have access to the inbox\"; (3) in inbox-config.ts set inboxNav to the screens you installed (numbers, rules, metrics, links), resolveUserNames() (same source as resolveUsers), contactAppHref() and inboxAgentNames; (4) replace sendo_can_access_tenant(tenant_id) in your database so operators only see their tenant; (5) mount <Toaster /> from components/ui/sonner in your root layout; (6) for live updates set NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL and NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and make lib/sendo-realtime.ts return a client with the operator's session. Set the language in lib/sendo-ui.ts (sendoLocale, \"en\" or \"es\"; pass formatLocale such as \"es-GT\" for regional dates and numbers) and override single texts with <Inbox strings={{ ... }} />; motion tokens live in components/sendo/motion.css (under prefers-reduced-motion opacity and colour still fade and transform movement is removed). See components/sendo/inbox/AGENTS.md."
